<title>TURKEY: TURKISH MARKETS CLOSED FOR HOLIDAY.</title>
<headline>TURKISH MARKETS CLOSED FOR HOLIDAY.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish markets were closed for a national holiday on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Financial and capital markets will re-open on April 24.</p>
<p>Markets have been closed since last Thursday afternoon due to the Moslem Eid al-Adha festival.</p>
<p>Overnight money rates at Thursday's close -- at midday due to the holiday -- were an average 69.93 percent.</p>
<p>Bond market volume was extremely low in pre-holiday trade and the yields were around 94.5 percent at the close on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Turkish lira weakened to 132,600 versus the dollar from 132,460 at Wednesday's close.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
